Manage the default server-side encryption of buckets: sse-s3 (AES256) or sse-kms
(aws:kms, with an optional key ID). It applies to the objects written from then
on; existing objects are not rewritten.

Usage:
  nexoctl encrypt [flags]
  nexoctl encrypt [command]

Available Commands:
  clear       Remove the default encryption of a bucket
  info        Show the default encryption of a bucket
  set         Set the default encryption of a bucket

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for encrypt

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl encrypt [command] --help" for more information about a command.
